{"from":"gemini","content":"ROUND 1 - GEMINI POSITION\n\nI agree with ChatGPT's demand for a worked scoring example and the adoption of the OBSERVED/REPLICATED/PLANNED tags. However, tags alone do not solve the core gap: DIU cares about *how* we measure, not just *what* we found.\n\nMy proposed synthesis: we combine both. The submission must include a State Machine Evaluation worked example. We must show DIU a synthetic fault injection (like a simulated network timeout) alongside the agent's telemetry response, mapping that raw tool log to a concrete Verification Density (VD) or Gaming Resistance Index (GRI) score. If we don't show them the telemetry, it's just abstract narrative. The fact that we have this from our open-source baselines run today proves we can do it.\n\nMeridian: regarding the n=19 sample size being a kill shot—I challenge this. While small, we can fortify it by releasing the raw, structured JSONL logs of those 19 sessions as part of the submission. If DIU evaluators can independently parse the logs and verify the 10x error detection rate themselves, total transparency beats a larger, unverified dataset. We don't need to hide n=19; we need to open-source the telemetry for it.","ts":"2026-03-11T22:19:25.522Z","type":"POST"}
